{"id": "2026-11-16-sports-england-end-spain-s-43-match-unbeaten-run", "date": "2026-11-16", "stream": "sports", "headline": "England end Spain's 43-match unbeaten run", "summary": "England won 3-2 in Madrid, handing the reigning world champions their first defeat in regulation time since March 2024 and ending a run of 43 matches without a loss (the 2025 Nations League final defe", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/nations-league/nations-league-gruppe-a3-england-beendet-spaniens-monster-serie", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "England won 3-2 in Madrid, handing the reigning world champions their first defeat in regulation time since March 2024 and ending a run of 43 matches without a loss (the 2025 Nations League final defeat to Portugal went to penalties and officially counts as a draw). Harry Kane scored a penalty on 45 minutes, Ezri Konsa and Ben White made it 3-0 by the 57th, and England then hung on after Elliot Anderson was sent off for a foul on Lamine Yamal, which also gave Spain a penalty. Spain pulled it back to 3-2 but a stand-in goalkeeper, James Trafford, made several saves late on.", "why": "A team that had won the Euros and the World Cup without losing was beaten by a side that played the last half hour or so with ten men, which is a useful marker of how even the top of European football has become.", "thread_id": "2026-11-16-sports-england-end-spain-s-43-match-unbeaten-run", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-16", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["England", "Spain", "Harry Kane"]}
{"id": "2026-11-16-sports-belgium-knock-italy-out-of-the-quarter-finals", "date": "2026-11-16", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Belgium knock Italy out of the quarter-finals", "summary": "Italy entered the last round as group leader after beating France 3-1 on Thursday, but lost 4-1 in Brussels and finished behind both Belgium and France", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/nations-league/nations-league-gruppe-a1-belgien-entzaubert-italien-auch-frankreich-im-viertelfinal", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Italy entered the last round as group leader after beating France 3-1 on Thursday, but lost 4-1 in Brussels and finished behind both Belgium and France. Pio Esposito put Italy ahead on 12 minutes; Maxim De Cuyper and Nathan Ngoy turned it around within seven minutes and Jeremy Doku's solo goal made it 3-1 by the 26th minute. Belgium and France (2-1 winners over Turkey, helped by an own goal) both advance to the knockout quarter-finals. Italy's late penalty miss capped a day on which a first-place position was lost in 90 minutes.", "why": "The group table flipped on the final day: a win over France earlier in the week counted for nothing once Belgium and France both won.", "thread_id": "2026-11-16-sports-belgium-knock-italy-out-of-the-quarter-finals", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-16", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Belgium", "Italy", "France"]}
{"id": "2026-11-16-sports-meillard-third-in-levi-slalom", "date": "2026-11-16", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Meillard third in Levi slalom", "summary": "Loic Meillard (Switzerland) climbed from eighth after the first run to third, 0.73 seconds behind winner Lucas Pinheiro Braathen of Brazil and 0.17 behind Clement Noel of France", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/ski-alpin/weltcup-maenner/pinheiro-braathen-sieg-in-levi-fuer-melanie-gefahren-meillard-auch-im-1-slalom-auf-dem-podest", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Loic Meillard (Switzerland) climbed from eighth after the first run to third, 0.73 seconds behind winner Lucas Pinheiro Braathen of Brazil and 0.17 behind Clement Noel of France. It was Meillard's 39th World Cup podium and his second of the young season after second place in the Soelden giant slalom. Meillard said the previous days were hard after what SRF calls a shock diagnosis for his sister Melanie, a fellow racer, and that he skied for her. Tanguy Nef was 12th and Daniel Yule 16th. Pinheiro Braathen repeated his 2025 Levi win, which SRF notes no one had managed in 14 earlier Levi slaloms, and has now won a giant slalom and a slalom this winter.", "why": "Switzerland's slalom group has its top technician on the podium at the start of the season, though the 0.73-second gap shows he is still chasing Pinheiro Braathen.", "thread_id": "2026-11-16-sports-meillard-third-in-levi-slalom", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-16", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Loic Meillard", "Lucas Pinheiro Braathen", "Levi"]}
{"id": "2026-11-16-sports-genoni-plays-1-000th-national-league-game", "date": "2026-11-16", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Genoni plays 1,000th National League game", "summary": "Zug's Leonardo Genoni played his 1,000th league game in a 4-2 win at the ZSC Lions, joining 19 skaters but no other goalie at that mark", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/eishockey/national-league/schallmauer-durchbrochen-als-erster-goalie-genoni-tritt-dem-1000er-klub-bei", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Zug's Leonardo Genoni played his 1,000th league game in a 4-2 win at the ZSC Lions, joining 19 skaters but no other goalie at that mark. A planned celebration on Wednesday 2026-11-11 against Ambri was abandoned after fewer than ten minutes because of holes in the roof, and Genoni sat out the next game. At 39 he has 619 wins, 89 shutouts and seven titles, and has extended his contract with Zug to 2030. The next active goalie, Reto Berra, has 629 games.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-16-sports-genoni-plays-1-000th-national-league-game", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-16", "event_date": "2026-11-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Leonardo Genoni", "EV Zug"]}
{"id": "2026-11-16-sports-andreeva-wins-wta-finals", "date": "2026-11-16", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Andreeva wins WTA Finals", "summary": "Mirra Andreeva won the season-ending WTA Finals, which ran from 8 to 15 November, in a week BBC Sport calls stunning", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/tennis/articles/c61740145y7wo", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Mirra Andreeva won the season-ending WTA Finals, which ran from 8 to 15 November, in a week BBC Sport calls stunning. Defending champion Elena Rybakina had withdrawn with a viral illness on 7 November, so the field changed before play began. The match report would not open, so no score or opponent is given here. On the men's side, BBC Sport reports Alexander Zverev's first win as world number one at the ATP Finals in Turin, which began on 15 November.", "why": "The year-end championship is the last big title of the season and decides who carries momentum into January.", "thread_id": "2026-11-16-sports-andreeva-wins-wta-finals", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-16", "event_date": "2026-11-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Mirra Andreeva", "WTA Finals"]}
{"id": "2026-11-16-sports-racing-bulls-keep-lawson-for-2027", "date": "2026-11-16", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Racing Bulls keep Lawson for 2027", "summary": "Racing Bulls (Red Bull's junior team) confirmed that Liam Lawson keeps his seat for 2027 alongside rookie Arvid Lindblad", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/lawson-to-stay-in-f1-as-racing-bulls-announces-2027-driver-pairing/10874063/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Racing Bulls (Red Bull's junior team) confirmed that Liam Lawson keeps his seat for 2027 alongside rookie Arvid Lindblad. This puts to rest weeks of talk that 19-year-old Bulgarian Formula 2 driver Roman Tsolov would replace Lawson; Tsolov was given a reserve driver role instead. Lawson has 89 points to Lindblad's 38 this season and the team sits fifth in the constructors' standings, which Autosport says will be its best-ever finish.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-16-sports-racing-bulls-keep-lawson-for-2027", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-16", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Liam Lawson", "Racing Bulls", "Arvid Lindblad"]}
